23:16:33 said  I decided: the brand name is **"GOLF AI"**, with a small red flag between the two words and "Golf AI Coach, Inc." underneath. I picked it because it matches your app's name, and it's easy to change.
23:16:33 said  I built a one-screen 3D site laid out like the original. The igloo is now a misty putting green with a red flag waving over the hole. There's also a golf ball, a curved putting line, and floating numbered points like the ones on the original. The text sits where the original's does: logo and copyright top-left, a sample mission statement top-right, and "Scroll down to discover" plus a sound button bottom-left. Scrolling moves the camera around the green and brings up three sample info panels with filler text. The last one links to your coach app, and the sound button plays a soft wind.
23:16:33 said  The automatic comparison rates it about 38% alike, well short of the 90% target. Almost all of that gap is the golf scene replacing the igloo, which you asked for, so I stopped trying to raise that number. The text positions match the original closely on tablet and phone. I never got a picture of the original's desktop text or of its scrolled sections, so I estimated the desktop text layout and made up the panel content.
23:16:33 said  Next, it would help to know your real app name, a one-line description, and a brand colour. With those I can replace the filler text and recolour the flag to match.
