02:13:59 said  I made the details more realistic:
02:13:59 said  - **Ball:** a dimpled surface under a glossy coat that catches reflections.
02:13:59 said  - **Flag:** woven cloth with a stitched sleeve, hemmed edges and a printed "18". It ripples, flutters at the tip in gusts and sags when the wind drops.
02:13:59 said  - **Grass:** the green has a real turf grain and a darker ring of longer grass at its edge, and the rough is thousands of individual blades swaying with the wind.
02:13:59 said  - **Sound:** gusting wind that follows the live wind reading, birdsong from left and right, a putter "tock" that's louder on longer putts, a rolling rumble while the ball moves, a rattle when it drops in, and soft ticks between slides.
02:14:00 said  My browser test caught a bug I fixed: turning sound on crashed and froze the scene. With sound on, the putting game, the scrolling putt and the carry-on-after-putting all pass without errors. I couldn't actually listen to the sounds, so give them a try. The match with the original stays about 28% alike, because of your app's colours.
